---
// Who, built from Eduardo's own concept mockup (who-mockup.html, pushed
// to the repo root and relocated into this page -- see public/concepts/
// and the removed root files in this same change). The copy below is
// transcribed verbatim from that mockup, not invented here: CLAUDE.md
// non-negotiable 1 is about never writing copy IN Eduardo's voice, and
// this is his own voice, supplied directly, not guessed at.
//
// Deliberately NOT carrying over the mockup's own top nav/sticky
// beamnav -- CLAUDE.md non-negotiable 2: the field is the only
// navigation, no second menu bar anywhere else on the site. This page
// keeps the same single "back to the field" convention writing.astro
// and every reader page already use, plus the same static .nerve-rest
// illusion at the top of the document (see writing.astro's own comment
// on why that exists as CSS, not a shared animated component).
import '../styles/global.css';
import Nameplate from '../components/Nameplate.astro';

// live-specimen.mov, named in the mockup bundle's own README.txt as the
// Who page's jellyfish footage, was never actually present in any of
// the three "Add files via upload" commits that delivered the rest of
// this bundle (confirmed directly: no .mov anywhere in the repo tree,
// not assumed missing). The transparent cutout the README names as this
// video's own fallback is real and ships here; the <video> element
// below points at a path that doesn't exist yet so swapping in the real
// file later is a one-line add, not a rebuild -- the poster image
// covers that gap until then exactly the way a fallback is supposed to.
const jellyfishVideo = '/concepts/live-specimen.mov';
const jellyfishPoster = '/concepts/data-jellyfish-cutout.png';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Who · EDUARDO sopalda</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="nerve-rest" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <Nameplate />
    <main>
      <p class="back"><a href="/">Back to the field</a></p>

      <header class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Who &middot; architect, operator, governance practitioner</p>
        <h1>Who<span class="dot">.</span></h1>
        <p class="pull">I don&rsquo;t make AI sound magical.<br />I make it operational.</p>
        <p class="dek">
          Architect by training. Global AI &amp; Data Governance Lead at dsm-firmenich. Still
          curious about what systems mean for people.
        </p>
        <a class="scroll" href="#throughline">&darr; Follow the throughline</a>

        <div class="hero-art">
          <img
            src="/concepts/annotated-brain-cutout.png"
            alt="A sculptural brain inscribed with data, curiosity, responsibility, reflection, AI and growth"
          />
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="section" id="throughline">
        <p class="label">01 &middot; The throughline</p>
        <h2>More than twenty years.<br />One recurring question.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          How do we make complex systems work for people&mdash;and keep responsibility human?
        </p>
        <p>
          For more than twenty years, I&rsquo;ve worked across solution architecture, global
          customer experience, technology operations, data quality, and governance. Different
          roles; one pattern: connect the technical system to the people who depend on it.
        </p>
        <p>
          My work has taken me from Barcelona to Tokyo, from Lima to New York. Across markets and
          disciplines, I keep returning to the same things: clear meaning, accountable systems,
          and trust earned in practice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section thread-section">
        <p class="label">Global experience &middot; Barcelona / Tokyo / Lima / New York</p>
        <h2>Networks. Architecture. AI. Governance.</h2>
        <ol class="threadline">
          <li>
            <b>Networks &amp; people</b>
            <p>
              I started in technical data analysis and incident operations for enterprise
              networks, working between customers and engineers across Europe and Asia, where
              reliability had to hold under pressure.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Architecture</b>
            <p>
              A different kind of systems thinking: how parts fit, how people move through
              spaces, and how a plan meets real constraints.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Trust &amp; AI quality</b>
            <p>
              Trust &amp; Safety, process optimization, and human-in-the-loop AI across
              multilingual teams. The work made feedback matter: a quality initiative raised KPIs
              by 15 points.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Governance</b>
            <p>
              Today, as D&amp;T Global Data Governance Lead at dsm-firmenich, I help turn
              policies into daily practice: clear ownership, trusted data, accountable AI.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <p class="label">02 &middot; Things I keep returning to</p>
        <h2>Some beliefs are less like answers than useful instruments.</h2>
        <div class="thought-list">
          <article class="thought">
            <small>01 &middot; Enable</small>
            <p>Good governance should enable, not merely mandate.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="thought">
            <small>02 &middot; Meaning</small>
            <p>People negotiate meaning. Systems should make that meaning usable.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="thought">
            <small>03 &middot; Accountability</small>
            <p>AI can assist a decision. It cannot take responsibility for its consequences.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section human">
        <div class="human-copy">
          <p class="label">
            03 &middot; Outside the title &middot; Still learning. That part doesn&rsquo;t stop.
          </p>
          <h2>People are the point.<br />Curiosity is the method.</h2>
          <p>
            I&rsquo;ve spent years close to the operational reality of technology: the customer
            waiting for a fix, the team interpreting a policy, the person expected to trust an AI
            system. That is why the work has to make sense to people, not only on paper.
          </p>
          <p>
            I contribute to DAMA Espa&ntilde;a&rsquo;s AI and Data Governance Working Group, write
            about the questions I meet in practice, and keep learning by building&mdash;most
            recently, exploring agentic AI from the inside.
          </p>
          <p class="pull-small">
            &ldquo;Data is our greatest asset.&rdquo;<br />
            <em>It&rsquo;s a good line. It&rsquo;s also wrong.<br />What&rsquo;s actually greatest: people.</em>
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="fish" aria-label="A floating jellyfish specimen in motion">
          <video autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="none" poster={jellyfishPoster} aria-hidden="true">
            <source src={jellyfishVideo} type="video/quicktime" />
          </video>
          <figcaption>Pelagic specimen &middot; data in motion</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="section end">
        <p class="label">A little more context</p>
        <h2>From architecture to AI governance.<br />Still asking what it means for people.</h2>
        <p>
          If you&rsquo;re here for the thinking, follow the Context. If you&rsquo;re here for the
          work, step into the Field.
        </p>
        <a class="cta" href="/context">Follow the Context &rarr;</a>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  html {
    overflow-y: auto;
    overflow-x: hidden;
  }

  body {
    overflow-y: auto;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    min-height: 100svh;
  }

  main {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 7rem;
    color: var(--bone);
  }

  .back a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--bone);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .back a:hover,
  .back a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .back a:focus-visible {
    outline: 1.5px solid var(--gold);
    outline-offset: 4px;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  .nerve-rest {
    position: fixed;
    top: calc(38px + env(safe-area-inset-top));
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      transparent,
      rgba(247, 197, 106, 0.55) 12%,
      rgba(247, 197, 106, 0.55) 88%,
      transparent
    );
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 5px rgba(247, 197, 106, 0.4));
    opacity: 0.75;
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 5;
    animation: nerve-rest-breathe 6.5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @keyframes nerve-rest-breathe {
    0%, 100% {
      opacity: 0.55;
      filter: drop-shadow(0 0 3px rgba(247, 197, 106, 0.3));
    }
    50% {
      opacity: 0.9;
      filter: drop-shadow(0 0 8px rgba(247, 197, 106, 0.55));
    }
  }

  .label {
    margin: 3rem 0 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(227, 175, 149, 0.6);
  }

  .hero {
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .hero .label {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 16vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.85;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  h1 .dot {
    color: var(--flesh);
  }

  .pull {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    max-width: 30rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--bone);
  }

  .dek {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    max-width: 30rem;
    font-family: var(--font-reading);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.7);
  }

  .scroll {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .scroll:hover,
  .scroll:focus-visible {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .hero-art {
    margin: 3rem 0 0;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 40%, rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.14), transparent 70%);
    border: 1px solid rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.12);
  }

  .hero-art img {
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 48vh;
    width: auto;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 18px 22px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55));
  }

  .section {
    padding-top: 4rem;
    margin-top: 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.12);
  }

  .section h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 5vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .section .lead {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--oxide-lit);
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  .section p {
    font-family: var(--font-reading);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.82);
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  .threadline {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  .threadline li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 1px solid rgba(210, 180, 111, 0.4);
  }

  .threadline li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -5px;
    top: 0.3rem;
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--void);
    border: 1px solid var(--gold);
  }

  .threadline b {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--bone);
  }

  .threadline p {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    max-width: 30rem;
  }

  .thought-list {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    background: rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.12);
    border: 1px solid rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.12);
  }

  .thought {
    background: var(--void);
    padding: 1.5rem 1.4rem;
  }

  .thought small {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bronze);
  }

  .thought p {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--champagne);
    max-width: none;
  }

  .human {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .pull-small {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--gold);
    max-width: 28rem;
  }

  .pull-small em {
    color: rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.75);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .fish {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .fish video {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 22rem;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 10px 22px rgba(210, 180, 111, 0.35));
  }

  .fish figcaption {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(227, 175, 149, 0.55);
  }

  .end {
    text-align: left;
  }

  .end p {
    max-width: 30rem;
  }

  .cta {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(210, 180, 111, 0.5);
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .cta:hover,
  .cta:focus-visible {
    background: rgba(210, 180, 111, 0.1);
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .human {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
      align-items: center;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .nerve-rest {
      animation: none;
      opacity: 0.75;
    }
  }
</style>
